## 2. CVE-2021-21402 + full Jellyfin CVE inventory

### CVE-2021-21402 (Jellyfin path traversal)
- NVD: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2021-21402 — published **2021-03-23**
- CVSS 3.1: **7.7 HIGH** (`AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:N/A:N`, NVD) and **6.5 MEDIUM** (`S:U`, GitHub/CNA); CVSSv2 4.0 (`Au:S`)
- NVD text: "In Jellyfin before version 10.7.1, with certain endpoints, well crafted requests will allow **arbitrary file read from a Jellyfin server's file system**. This issue is more prevalent when **Windows** is used as the host OS. Servers that are exposed to the public Internet are potentially at risk."
- GHSA-wg4c-c9g9-rxhx (https://github.com/jellyfin/jellyfin/security/advisories/GHSA-wg4c-c9g9-rxhx): severity **Moderate**; affected ≤10.7.0; patched **10.7.1, released 2021-03-21**. Vulnerable controllers named: **`ImageByNameController`, `SubtitleController`/`SubtitleManager`, `HlsSegmentController`** (one commit also references an *authenticated* arbitrary file **overwrite** in SubtitleController).
- Fix commit: `0183ef8e89195f420c48d2600bc0b72f6d3a7fd7`
- **Note the CVSS disagreement is load-bearing**: the CVE vector says `PR:L` (some privilege), but the vulnerable controllers are exactly the ones #5415 documents as *unauthenticated*.

